================================================================================
                              ATTRIBUTION REQUIREMENTS
================================================================================

1. GENERAL ATTRIBUTION:
   The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in 
   all copies or substantial portions of the Software.

2. COMPILED SOFTWARE ATTRIBUTION:
   Any software compiled using the LayerCake compiler that is distributed 
   publicly must include one of the following attribution notices:

   - In software documentation: "Compiled with LayerCake Compiler"
   - In application credits/about section: "Built with LayerCake"
   - In command-line tools help: "--version output must mention LayerCake"
   - In library documentation: "Created using LayerCake language"

3. DERIVATIVE WORKS ATTRIBUTION:
   Any derivative compiler, language, or development tool based on LayerCake 
   must clearly indicate its relationship to LayerCake and cannot use the 
   name "LayerCake" or confusingly similar names.

4. REDISTRIBUTION REQUIREMENTS:
   Redistributions must maintain the original name "LayerCake" and cannot
   be renamed to avoid attribution or create confusion about origin.

